&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage critical breakdowns:&lt;/strong&gt; You coordinate your team during technical issues and work closely with Operations to minimize downtime.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive safety &amp;amp; structure:&lt;/strong&gt; You ensure that safety standards are followed and that maintenance work is carried out in a clean and structured environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive continuous improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; You identify improvement opportunities and implement Lean, 5S and Continuous Improvement initiatives together with your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate across teams:&lt;/strong&gt; You work closely with Operations, Maintenance Engineers and external maintenance partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive salary with growth potential:&lt;/strong&gt; Starting at €70,000 gross/year, with annual performance reviews designed to drive your personal and financial development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a completed technical qualification with further training as a Technician or Master Craftsman, or a completed technical degree (Bachelor/Master), for example in Mechatronics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 10+ years of experience in a technical or maintenance environment, ideally within an automated, logistics or production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 3 years of leadership experience, for example as a Team Lead, Lead Technician, Supervisor or in a comparable role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a hands-on mindset and understand both the technical and operational side of maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with Lean, 5S and Continuous Improvement and enjoy applying these principles on the shop floor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work in a structured way, take ownership and stay calm and focused during critical breakdowns&lt;/li&gt;
